; bfsodium CBCENC128 : AES_128 in cipher block chaining mode  encryption only
; NIST SP 800_38A section 6 point 2
;
; NOTE square brackets are brainfuck loops  so comments use braces for counts;
;
; HAND WRITTEN; block/aes128table block/aes128encrypt block/copy16 and
; block/copy16back are INCLUDED; idiom/xor8 is PASTED; Like aes/ctr128 this
; file is the plumbing of a mode and owns no round and no S box;
;
; IO  in:  key{16}  iv{16}  len{2} LE  plaintext{len}
;     out: ciphertext{len}
;
; LEN MUST BE A MULTIPLE OF SIXTEEN; cipher block chaining is defined on whole
; blocks and this file does no padding  because padding is a choice a caller
; makes and a primitive that made it for them would be the wrong primitive;
; A length that is not a multiple of sixteen reads sixteen bytes anyway and
; takes the count below nought  so the caller is the one that must be right;
; That is stated here rather than enforced: the check costs instructions on
; every run to catch a caller error that the vectors cannot produce;
;
; THE LENGTH PREFIX is how the program knows when to stop; a bfsodium
; primitive never relies on end of input;
;
; ENCRYPTION ONLY  AND THE DECRYPTION IS NOT NEXT DOOR; CBC is the one mode in
; the roster that needs the INVERSE cipher  and block/aes128decrypt cannot be
; included twice: it lays the forward table  spends it on the key schedule
; clears it and writes the inverse one into the same cells  then runs the
; rounds; There is no prefix of it a caller can run once; Its header says what
; restructuring decryption will need; This file needs none of that  because
; CBC ENCRYPTION USES THE FORWARD CIPHER  exactly as counter mode does;
;
; WHAT CHAINING COSTS OVER COUNTING  and it is almost nothing: counter mode
; encrypts a counter it owns  this one encrypts the plaintext exclusive ored
; with the previous ciphertext; So the per block work is the same cipher and
; the same restoration  and the only new thing is that the block being fed in
; comes from the wire rather than from an increment;
;
; THE CHAIN IS A CONVEYOR  which is how the exclusive or stays one paste; The
; chain's head byte is always at @0x3c7: it is lifted out  the other fifteen
; slide down  and the result of the exclusive or goes in at the tail; Sixteen
; turns later the chain is back in its original order holding the whole block;
; The alternative was sixteen pastes of idiom/xor8 at sixteen fixed offsets
; which is the shape HANDOFF calls indices rather than conveyors;
;
; THE TAPE IS LAID OUT EXACTLY AS aes/ctr128 LAYS IT  down to the cell: the
; key sits 885 above the window and the chain sits 885 above the state; That
; was a deliberate choice in the first mode and this is the file that collects
; on it  having cost nothing to make;
;
; ONE DISTANCE  TWO ROUTINES  AND THE DIFFERENCE IS NOT SPEED; the key is
; COPIED with block/copy16 because every block wants it again; the chain is
; MOVED with block/move16 because it is SPENT the moment it reaches the state;
; the next chaining value is the ciphertext that comes back; Writing that
; second one as a copy leaves the chained plaintext standing where the
; ciphertext is about to be moved in  and a move into an occupied cell ADDS;
; The first block is still right  because a block is emitted before it is
; chained  so only a message of TWO BLOCKS OR MORE can show it; The contract
; below the cipher now says the chain is empty  and that is the line that
; would have caught it on the first run;
;
; THE WINDOW AND THE ROUND CONSTANT ARE PUT BACK at the head of every block
; for the reason block/aes128encrypt's own contract now states: the schedule
; spends the window and leaves the constant at 0x6c;
;
; TAPE MAP  (home @0)
;   @0x000:0x374  THE CIPHER'S FRAME  exactly as block/aes128encrypt maps it
;     @0x000:0x00f  window{16}   the key is COPIED in at every block
;     @0x010:0x01f  ALSO the key copy's staging cells
;     @0x02d        rcon  CLEARED at every block
;     @0x052:0x061  state{16}  the chained block in  the ciphertext out
;     @0x062:0x071  the round key  and NOTHING of this mode's  because the
;                   chain is moved rather than copied and has no stage
;     @0x075:0x374  the S box  laid ONCE by block/aes128table
;   @0x375:0x384  savedkey{16}  the key as it came off the wire  never spent
;   @0x3c7:0x3d6  chain{16}  the IV  then each ciphertext block in turn
;   @0x3d8:0x3d9  remaining{2} u16 LE  message bytes still to read
;   @0x3da        nz     set while remaining is not zero
;   @0x3db        bcnt   bytes still to take into this block  starts at 16
;   @0x3dc        e      the else arm of the borrowing decrement
;   @0x3dd        t      a copy  so a count can be tested without being eaten
;   @0x3de        u      puts that copy back
;   @0x3df:0x3ef  idiom/xor8 pasted at 991; result 991  operands 992 and 993
;
; THE GAP AT @0x385:0x3c6 IS NOT WASTE  for the reason aes/ctr128 records: it
; is what puts the chain exactly 885 cells above the state;

; ==== the key  the initialisation vector and the length ====
; a read prologue may only ever move right  so each operand is read where
; it lives rather than read low and moved up
R885
  ,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,
; ASSERT ptr=900
R67
; ASSERT ptr=967
  ,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,
; ASSERT ptr=982
