; ==== the ciphertext goes out  and becomes the next chain ====
; emitting does not spend a cell and the move does  so each byte leaves and
; then goes up to the chain  which empties the state for the next block
; THE CHAIN MUST BE EMPTY HERE and the contract below is not decoration: a
; move into an occupied cell ADDS  so if the chained block were still
; standing the next chaining value would be the sum of it and the
; ciphertext; This file did exactly that until the two block vector failed
